GHOST_SDL: ask for an OpenGL 3.3 core profile context

GHOST_SDL asks SDL for OpenGL 3.3 with profile mask 0 (no profile), for windows and for offscreen
contexts. Haiku's SDL2 (with the haiku-pi glview-core patch) creates a core profile context only for
SDL_GL_CONTEXT_PROFILE_CORE; a request without a profile gets the compatibility context, which on
V3D 4.2 is OpenGL 3.1, and Blender 3.6 then stops with "Platform Unsupported" (it needs 3.3).
Blender's GPU module uses only core-profile functionality, as GHOST's other backends request
(GHOST_ContextGLX/EGL/WGL/CGL ask for core 3.3). docs/design/blender.md §3.3.

diff --git a/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_SystemSDL.cc b/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_SystemSDL.cc
index 52c222c..6b784c7 100644
--- a/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_SystemSDL.cc
+++ b/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_SystemSDL.cc
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ GHOST_IContext *GHOST_SystemSDL::createOffscreenContext(GHOST_GLSettings /*glSet
 {
   GHOST_Context *context = new GHOST_ContextSDL(false,
                                                 nullptr,
-                                                0, /* Profile bit. */
+                                                SDL_GL_CONTEXT_PROFILE_CORE,
                                                 3,
                                                 3,
                                                 GHOST_OPENGL_SDL_CONTEXT_FLAGS,
